id           = CWE-1253
name         = Incorrect Selection of Fuse Values
abstraction  = Base
structure    = Simple
status       = Draft

description : The logic level used to set a system to a secure state relies on a fuse being unblown.

extended description : Fuses are often used to store secret data, including security configuration data. When not blown, a fuse is considered to store a logic 0, and, when blown, it indicates a logic 1. Fuses are generally considered to be one-directional, i.e., once blown to logic 1, it cannot be reset to logic 0.

notes : https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1253.html
